zoom: the CSS zoom property. Its computed value here is the effective zoom (the product of the element's own zoom and
its ancestors'), so it is registered as inherited; each element's density-independent pixel ratio carries it, which
scales every dp, viewport and rem length, inherited absolute font sizes and line heights, decorators, effects and
replaced-element natural sizes. A zero zoom is no zoom.
CSS Viewport 1: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-viewport/#zoom-property

